<http://data.silknow.org/production/3c705692-426d-3b33-8ca6-55c0af45e6ef>
        a                       ecrm:E12_Production ;
        rdfs:comment            "The printer is credited as: 'Hiscoke and Son, Printers, Stamp office, Richmond.'  Hiscoke and Son were the publishers of the books <i>An Essay on Music</i>, by Dr Sellé, c.1880, and <i>The History and Antiquities of Richmond, Kew, Petersham, Ham Etc</i>.  When they published the book on Dr Sellé, Hiscoke and Son were in Hill Street, Richmond, Surrey." ;
        ecrm:P108_has_produced  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7d200ecb-416f-33e5-b1a2-1e502080ebea> ;
        ecrm:P126_employed      "printing ink"@en , "silk (textile)"@en , "Printed silk"@en , "ink"@en ;
        ecrm:P32_used_general_technique
                "printed"@en ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note        "The printer is credited as: 'Hiscoke and Son, Printers, Stamp office, Richmond.'  Hiscoke and Son were the publishers of the books <i>An Essay on Music</i>, by Dr Sellé, c.1880, and <i>The History and Antiquities of Richmond, Kew, Petersham, Ham Etc</i>.  When they published the book on Dr Sellé, Hiscoke and Son were in Hill Street, Richmond, Surrey." ;
